<problem>
<!-- <title>Calculate stability of equilibria of differential equation analytically</title> -->


<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from="-10" to=" 10" exclude="0" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="true" />

<select name="x">x y z s u v w</select>

<function name="quad_factored" variables="$x" symbolic="true">
  <math simplify="number">$x *($a[1] *$x +$a[2] )</math>
</function>
<function name="quad" variables="$x" symbolic="true">
  <math expand="true" simplify="true">$quad_factored</math>
</function>
<function name="fun" variables="$x" symbolic="true">$$quad($x )*e^(-$x )</function>

<math name="fun_xe" simplify="numbers">$$fun($(x)_e )</math>
<math name="quad_xe" simplify="numbers">$$quad($(x)_e )</math>
<math name="quad_factored_xe" simplify="numbers">$$quad_factored($(x)_e )</math>

<mathList name="Es">
  <sort name="E1">
    <math>0</math>
    <math simplify="numbers">-$a[2] /$a[1]</math>
  </sort>
</mathList>

<function name="fprime" variables="$x">
  <math simplify="numbers">
    (-$a[1] *$x^2 + (2$a[1]-$a[2])*$x +$a[2])*e^(-$x )
  </math>
</function>
  
<evaluate name="fprime_E1" function="$fprime" input="$E1[1]" displayDigits="5" />
<boolean name="E1_stable">$fprime_E1  &lt; 0</boolean>

<evaluate name="fprime_E2" function="$fprime" input="$E1[2]" displayDigits="5" />
<boolean name="E2_stable">$fprime_E2  &lt; 0</boolean>

<textList name="EstabilityText">
  <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$E1_stable">
      <text>stable</text>
    </case>
    <else>
      <text>unstable</text>
    </else>
  </conditionalContent>
  <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$E2_stable">
      <text>stable</text>
    </case>
    <else>
      <text>unstable</text>
    </else>
  </conditionalContent>
</textList>
  
<math name="xmax" simplify="numbers">max(2.2,max(abs($E1[1]),abs($E1[2]))*1.3)</math>
<math name="xmin" simplify="numbers">-$xmax </math>
<math name="min_abs_f_special_points" simplify="full" unordered="true">min(abs($$fun($xmin )),abs($$fun($xmax )),abs($$fun(($E1[1] +$E1[2] )/2)))</math>
<function name="fun_rescaled" variables="x">$$fun($x )/$min_abs_f_special_points *3</function>


  
    <styleDefinition styleNumber="2" lineWidth="3" />
    <styleDefinition styleNumber="9" markerColor="red" markerStyle="circle" markerSize="5" />
  
  
</setup>


For the dynamical system
<me>\frac{ d$x }{ dt } = <math extend="$fun.formula" />,</me>
find all equilibria and analytically determine their stability (i.e., use the stability theorem).  Using this information, draw a phase line diagram with equilibria and vector field.  Use solid circles for stable equilibria and open circles for unstable equilibria.

<p>Number of equilibria: <mathInput name="n_e" /></p>

<p>Equilibria (in increasing order): </p>

  <ul>
    <repeatForSequence length="min($n_e,5)" name="esMap" valueName="v"><li><m>$(x)_e=</m> <mathInput /></li></repeatForSequence>
  </ul>
  
<p>
<answer matchPartial="true" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001">
  <award>
    <when>
      <mathList name="uEs" isResponse="true"><setup><collect componentType="mathInput" from="$esMap" name="collect_list" /></setup><mathList name="list" extend="$collect_list.value" /></mathList>
      = $Es
    </when>
  </award>
  <award unorderedCompare="true" credit="0.8" name="award2">
    <when>
      $uEs = $Es
    </when>
  </award>
</answer>
</p>

<feedback condition="$award2">Enter equilibria in increasing order for full credit.</feedback>

  

<p>Stability of equilibria:</p>

<ul>
<repeat for="$uEs" name="mapStab" valueName="v"><li><m>$(x)_e=$v</m> is 
    <choiceInput inline="true">
      <choice>stable</choice>
      <choice>unstable</choice>
    </choiceInput>
    </li>
  </repeat>
</ul>
<p>
<answer>
  <award matchPartial="true" matchByExactPositions="true">
    <when>
      <textList><setup><collect componentType="choiceInput" from="$mapStab" name="collect_list1" /></setup><textList name="list1" extend="$collect_list1.selectedValue" /></textList>
      = $EstabilityText
    </when>
  </award>
</answer>
</p>


<!-- <copy uri="doenet:activityId=83TXioRLQfjiFmpyoM1xhD" aspectRatio="10/3" var="$x" nEquilibria="2" E1="$E1" E2="$E2" E1stable="$E1_stable" vmin="$xmin" vmax="$xmax" attractThreshold="0.1" /> -->

<module copy="doenet:83TXioRLQfjiFmpyoM1xhD" aspectRatio="10/3" var="$x" nEquilibria="2" E1="$E1[1]" E2="$E1[2]" E1stable="$E1_stable" vmin="$xmin" vmax="$xmax" attractThreshold="0.1" />

<solution>
  <setup>

<math name="fprime_sub" simplify="numbers">
  (2 $a[1] *$x +$a[2])e^(-$x) - ($a[1] *$x^2 +$a[2] $x ) e^(-$x)
</math>
    
  </setup>
  
<p>Let <m>f($x ) = <math extend="$fun.formula" /></m>.  The equilibria are points where <m>\frac{ d$x }{ dt }=0</m>, i.e., where 
<m>f($x ) = 0</m>.  If <m>$x _e</m> is an equilibrium, then the equilibrium must satisfy
<me>$fun_xe =0.</me>
Since the exponential cannot be zero, the only possibilities are that
<me>$quad_xe =0</me>
or
<me>$quad_factored_xe =0.</me>
Therefore the equilibria are <m>$x _e=$E1[1] </m> and <m>$x _e=$E1[2] </m>.</p>

<p>To determine stability, we need to evaluate the derivative of <m>f</m> at the equilibria.  Using the product rule, 
<md>
  <mrow>f'($x )\amp = $fprime_sub"</mrow>
  <mrow>\amp = <math extend="$fprime.formula" />.</mrow>
</md>
Since 
<me>f'($E1[1] ) = $fprime_E1
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E1_stable">
\lt 
</case>
<else>
\gt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
0,</me>
the equilibrium <m>$x _e=$E1[1] </m> is
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E1_stable">stable</case>
<else>unstable</else>
</conditionalContent>.
Since 
<me>f'\left($E1[2] \right) = $fprime_E2 
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E2_stable">
\lt 
</case>
<else>
\gt 
</else>
</conditionalContent>
0,</me>
the equilibrium <m>$x _e=$E1[2] </m> is
<conditionalContent>
<case condition="$E2_stable">stable</case>
<else>unstable</else>
</conditionalContent>.  
</p>


<p>To draw the vector field, draw the arrows toward the stable equilibrium and away from the unstable equilibrium.  The resulting phase line is shown below.</p>


  <graph aspectRatio="50/15" xmin="$xmin" xmax="$xmax" ymin="-3" ymax="3" fixAxes="true">
    <xLabel><m>$x</m></xLabel>
    <equilibriumPoint styleNumber="9" stable="$E1_stable" fixed="true">($E1[1], 0)</equilibriumPoint>
    <equilibriumPoint styleNumber="9" stable="$E2_stable" fixed="true">($E1[2], 0)</equilibriumPoint>

    <conditionalContent>
      <case condition="$E1_stable">
        <vector styleNumber="2" tail="($xmin+0.1, 0)" head="($E1[1]-0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
        <vector styleNumber="2" tail="($E1[2]-0.1, 0)" head="($E1[1]+0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
        <vector styleNumber="2" tail="($E1[2]+0.1, 0)" head="($xmax-0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
      </case>
      <else>
        <vector styleNumber="2" head="($xmin+0.1, 0)" tail="($E1[1]-0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
        <vector styleNumber="2" head="($E1[2]-0.1, 0)" tail="($E1[1]+0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
        <vector styleNumber="2" head="($E1[2]+0.1, 0)" tail="($xmax-0.1,0)" fixed="true" />
      </else>
    </conditionalContent>
    
  </graph>




</solution>


</problem>